{"name":"Oxley","hex":"#6d9a78","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Oxley","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Wolverhampton, West Midlands, England .","A community in the town of Essex, Essex County, Ontario, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Oxley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oxley, Australian Capital Territory","blocks":[{"text":"Oxley is the smallest suburb in Canberra. It is located in the district of Tuggeranong. The suburb is named after the explorer John Joseph William Molesworth Oxley, who explored parts of New South Wales. It was gazetted on 22 March 1982 and first settled in 1985. Streets are named after social reformers and the suburb has an area of 1.08 km2."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxley%2C_Australian_Capital_Territory","wikidata":"Q1227239"},{"title":"Oxley, Queensland","blocks":[{"text":"Oxley is a south-western suburb in the City of Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. It is 14.8 kilometres (9.2 mi) from the Brisbane GPO by road. The suburb contains a mix of residential and industrial land. In the 2021 census, Oxley had a population of 9,100 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Oxley_central_roundabout.jpg/330px-Oxley_central_roundabout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxley%2C_Queensland","wikidata":"Q7115680"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ipswich_Motorway_looking_west_at_Oxley_Road_roundabout%2C_Oxley%2C_Queensland.jpg/500px-Ipswich_Motorway_looking_west_at_Oxley_Road_roundabout%2C_Oxley%2C_Queensland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Ipswich_Motorway_looking_west_at_Oxley_Road_roundabout%2C_Oxley%2C_Queensland.jpg/1280px-Ipswich_Motorway_looking_west_at_Oxley_Road_roundabout%2C_Oxley%2C_Queensland.jpg?ut